@prefix : <http://purl.org/csf/frames#> .
@prefix csf: <http://purl.org/csf/> .
@prefix core: <http://purl.org/csf/core#> .
@prefix frm: <http://purl.org/csf/frames#> .
@prefix csc: <http://purl.org/csf/cascades#> .
@prefix out: <http://purl.org/csf/outcomes#> .
@prefix pol: <http://purl.org/polanyi/heuristics#> .
@prefix fschema: <https://w3id.org/framester/schema/> .
@prefix dul: <http://www.ontologydesignpatterns.org/ont/dul/DUL.owl#> .
@prefix owl: <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#> .
@prefix rdf: <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#> .
@prefix rdfs: <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#> .
@prefix xsd: <http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#> .
@prefix skos: <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#> .
@prefix dcterms: <http://purl.org/dc/terms/> .

csf:frames
    a owl:Ontology ;
    owl:imports csf:core ;
    dcterms:title "CSF Frames Module"@en ;
    owl:versionInfo "3.3.0" ;
    dcterms:description """Frame definitions for the CSF ontology network. Contains two frame 
    families aligned via fschema:Frame and dul:Description:
    
    CORTICOIDOGENIC FRAMES (A-G): Situation-type descriptions that characterize life 
    conditions structurally predisposed to chronic HPA axis activation. Each frame 
    specifies core and peripheral semantic roles (CSFRole subclasses) following 
    Fillmorean frame semantics. Situations EVOKE corticoidogenic frames (D&S pattern):
        A. ChronicSubordinationFrame    (McEwen 1998, PMID 9629234)
        B. UncontrollableThreatFrame    (Herman 2020, PMID 33345670)
        C. CaregivingEntrapmentFrame    (Kiecolt-Glaser 1991, PMID 1656478)
        D. EarlyLifeProgrammingFrame    (Weaver 2004, PMID 15220929)
        E. ChronicIdentityThreatFrame   (Slavich & Irwin 2014, PMID 24417575)
        F. CircadianMisalignmentFrame   (Scheer et al. 2009, PMID 19255424)
        G. SocialDisconnectionFrame     (Cole 2007, PMID 17854483)
    
    PROTECTIVE FRAMES (P1-P4, v3.3): Frame types that characterize conditions under 
    which cascade severity is attenuated or redirected toward resilience outcomes. 
    Added in v3.3 to address the systematic via-negativa commitment identified by 
    the DARKSIDE audit (Req 11): the ontology previously modeled only harm pathways 
    with no resilience, coping, or recovery frames.
    
    Protective frames are NOT inverse corticoidogenic frames. They are distinct frame 
    types that MODULATE ongoing cascades rather than triggering cascades of their own. 
    This avoids the error of treating resilience as merely 'negative stress.' They 
    operate at the situation-cascade interface via frm:bufferedByFrame (the positive-
    pathway counterpart to csf:evokes):
        P1. SocialSupportFrame          (Hostinar et al. 2014, PMID 23607429)
        P2. AgencyRestorationFrame      (Deci & Ryan 2000, PMID 11392867)
        P3. CulturalContinuityFrame     (Chandler & Lalonde 2008)
        P4. MeaningMakingFrame          (Park 2010, PMID 20192563)
    
    ARCHITECTURAL NOTES:
    - ProtectiveFrame is subClassOf CorticoidogenicFrame for taxonomic coherence 
      (both are fschema:Frame, dul:Description), not because protective frames are 
      stress-inducing. An alternative design with a common CSFFrame superclass was 
      considered but rejected for backward compatibility.
    - Each frame specifies frm:buffersAgainstFrame → CorticoidogenicFrame to indicate 
      which harm pathways it attenuates, and frm:protectiveStrength (xsd:float 0-1) 
      for estimated attenuation magnitude.
    - Protective frame strength values are literature-informed estimates, not 
      empirically calibrated parameters. They should be treated as prior defaults 
      subject to Bayesian updating from clinical data.
    """@en ;
    rdfs:comment """v3.3 / Req 11 (H1 — Protective Frames): This module now contains both 
    corticoidogenic and protective frames. The addition of protective frames addresses 
    three identified gaps:
    
    1. RESILIENCE EXCLUSION (DARKSIDE trail): All 14 CSF_Situation types previously 
       evoked only harm/stress frames. No situation could link to a protective or 
       recovery description. Protective frames restore this missing pathway via 
       frm:bufferedByFrame, enabling situations to be simultaneously classified as 
       stressful (via csf:evokes) and buffered (via frm:bufferedByFrame).
    
    2. MODERATOR-FRAME DISCONNECT: mod:Buffer individuals in csf-moderators.ttl 
       attenuated cascade severity but had no frame-level representation. Protective 
       frames provide the schema-level description that buffers instantiate — e.g., 
       mod:HighSocialSupport is an instance of the SocialSupportFrame's protective 
       pattern, and int:PeerSupportProgram (H7) activates SocialSupportFrame via 
       int:activatesProtectiveFrame.
    
    3. OUTCOME TRAJECTORY ASYMMETRY: csf:typicallyLeadsTo linked cascade frames only 
       to negative ClinicalOutcome classes. With protective frames, the cascade can 
       be redirected toward csf:ResilienceOutcome and csf:RecoveryOutcome (defined 
       in csf-core.ttl v3.1) via csf:hasProtectiveTrajectory.
    
    The four protective frame types were selected based on meta-analytic evidence for 
    HPA axis buffering effects: social buffering via oxytocin-mediated pathways 
    (Hostinar et al. 2014); perceived control and self-determination reducing cortisol 
    reactivity (Deci & Ryan 2000; Dickerson & Kemeny 2004); cultural continuity as 
    protective against suicide and allostatic load in Indigenous and immigrant 
    populations (Chandler & Lalonde 2008); and meaning-making / cognitive reappraisal 
    reducing cortisol via prefrontal regulation of amygdala (Park 2010).
    
    KNOWN LIMITATION: The protectiveStrength values (0.45-0.60) are aggregate estimates.
    In reality, protective frame effectiveness is moderated by: (a) timing relative to 
    GAS phase (H2b) — social support is more effective in Resistance than Exhaustion; 
    (b) match between protective frame type and stressor type — CulturalContinuity 
    specifically buffers IdentityThreat, not CircadianMisalignment; (c) dose — 
    intermittent vs. sustained buffering. These interaction effects are partially 
    captured via the frm:buffersAgainstFrame specificity but not via dose-response 
    modeling, which is deferred to future work."""@en ;
    pol:designHeuristic pol:b01-FRAMEBINDING ;
    rdfs:seeAlso 
        <https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/23607429/> ,
        <https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/11392867/> ,
        <https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/20192563/> .

frm:typicalCascade a owl:ObjectProperty .
frm:typicalSeverity a owl:ObjectProperty .
frm:typicalOutcomes a owl:ObjectProperty .
frm:compoundsWithFrame a owl:ObjectProperty .
csf:hasCSFRole a owl:ObjectProperty .

# ==========================================
# TYPE A: CHRONIC SUBORDINATION
# ==========================================
frm:ChronicSubordinationFrame a csf:CorticoidogenicFrame, owl:NamedIndividual ;
    rdfs:label "Chronic Subordination Frame"@en ;
    csf:hasCSFRole csf:Experiencer, csf:Stressor, csf:Context,
                   frm:HierarchyStructure, frm:StatusPosition, frm:DominanceBehavior ;
    csf:pubmedID "9629234" ;
    csf:evidenceStrength "systematic-review" ;
    frm:typicalCascade csc:SubordinationCascade ;
    frm:typicalSeverity csf:Moderate, csf:High ;
    frm:typicalOutcomes out:Depression, out:Anxiety, out:MetabolicSyndrome, out:Burnout .

frm:HierarchyStructure a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:subClassOf csf:CSFRole ,
        [ a owl:Restriction ; owl:onProperty csf:coreElement ; owl:hasValue "true"^^xsd:boolean ] ;
    rdfs:label "Hierarchy Structure"@en .

frm:StatusPosition a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:subClassOf csf:CSFRole ,
        [ a owl:Restriction ; owl:onProperty csf:coreElement ; owl:hasValue "true"^^xsd:boolean ] ;
    rdfs:label "Status Position"@en .

frm:DominanceBehavior a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:subClassOf csf:CSFRole ,
        [ a owl:Restriction ; owl:onProperty csf:coreElement ; owl:hasValue "false"^^xsd:boolean ] ;
    rdfs:label "Dominance Behavior"@en .

# ==========================================
# TYPE B: UNCONTROLLABLE THREAT
# ==========================================
frm:UncontrollableThreatFrame a csf:CorticoidogenicFrame, owl:NamedIndividual ;
    rdfs:label "Uncontrollable Threat Frame"@en ;
    csf:hasCSFRole csf:Experiencer, csf:Stressor, csf:Context,
                   frm:ThreatSource, frm:ResponseFutility, frm:VigilanceRequirement ;
    csf:pubmedID "33345670" ;
    frm:typicalCascade csc:UncontrollableThreatCascade ;
    frm:typicalSeverity csf:High, csf:VeryHigh ;
    frm:typicalOutcomes out:PTSD, out:ComplexTrauma, out:TreatmentResistantDepression, out:Dissociation .

frm:ThreatSource a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:subClassOf csf:CSFRole ,
        [ a owl:Restriction ; owl:onProperty csf:coreElement ; owl:hasValue "true"^^xsd:boolean ] ;
    rdfs:label "Threat Source"@en .

frm:ResponseFutility a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:subClassOf csf:CSFRole ,
        [ a owl:Restriction ; owl:onProperty csf:coreElement ; owl:hasValue "true"^^xsd:boolean ] ;
    rdfs:label "Response Futility"@en .

frm:VigilanceRequirement a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:subClassOf csf:CSFRole ,
        [ a owl:Restriction ; owl:onProperty csf:coreElement ; owl:hasValue "false"^^xsd:boolean ] ;
    rdfs:label "Vigilance Requirement"@en .

# ==========================================
# TYPE C: CAREGIVING ENTRAPMENT
# ==========================================
frm:CaregivingEntrapmentFrame a csf:CorticoidogenicFrame, owl:NamedIndividual ;
    rdfs:label "Caregiving Entrapment Frame"@en ;
    csf:hasCSFRole csf:Experiencer, csf:Stressor, csf:Context,
                   frm:CareRecipient, frm:CaregivingDemand, frm:SupportDeficit, 
                   frm:RoleEndpoint, frm:AmbiguousLoss ;
    csf:pubmedID "1656478" ;
    frm:compoundsWithFrame frm:CircadianMisalignmentFrame ;
    frm:typicalCascade csc:CaregivingEntrapmentCascade ;
    frm:typicalSeverity csf:High, csf:VeryHigh ;
    frm:typicalOutcomes out:Depression, out:CaregiverBurnout, out:ImmuneDysregulation .

frm:CareRecipient a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:subClassOf csf:CSFRole ,
        [ a owl:Restriction ; owl:onProperty csf:coreElement ; owl:hasValue "true"^^xsd:boolean ] ;
    rdfs:label "Care Recipient"@en .

frm:CaregivingDemand a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:subClassOf csf:CSFRole ,
        [ a owl:Restriction ; owl:onProperty csf:coreElement ; owl:hasValue "true"^^xsd:boolean ] ;
    rdfs:label "Caregiving Demand"@en .

frm:SupportDeficit a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:subClassOf csf:CSFRole ,
        [ a owl:Restriction ; owl:onProperty csf:coreElement ; owl:hasValue "false"^^xsd:boolean ] ;
    rdfs:label "Support Deficit"@en .

frm:RoleEndpoint a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:subClassOf csf:CSFRole ,
        [ a owl:Restriction ; owl:onProperty csf:coreElement ; owl:hasValue "false"^^xsd:boolean ] ;
    rdfs:label "Role Endpoint"@en .

frm:AmbiguousLoss a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:subClassOf csf:CSFRole ,
        [ a owl:Restriction ; owl:onProperty csf:coreElement ; owl:hasValue "false"^^xsd:boolean ] ;
    rdfs:label "Ambiguous Loss"@en .

# ==========================================
# TYPE D: EARLY LIFE PROGRAMMING
# ==========================================
frm:EarlyLifeProgrammingFrame a csf:CorticoidogenicFrame, owl:NamedIndividual ;
    rdfs:label "Early Life Programming Frame"@en ;
    csf:hasCSFRole csf:Experiencer, csf:Stressor, csf:Context,
                   frm:DevelopmentalWindow, frm:Caregiver, frm:AttachmentQuality,
                   frm:EpigeneticModification, frm:HPASetPoint ;
    csf:pubmedID "15220929" ;
    frm:compoundsWithFrame frm:UncontrollableThreatFrame ;
    frm:typicalCascade csc:EarlyLifeProgrammingCascade ;
    frm:typicalSeverity csf:VeryHigh ;
    frm:typicalOutcomes out:LifelongVulnerability, out:RecurrentDepression, out:PTSD .

frm:DevelopmentalWindow a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:subClassOf csf:CSFRole ,
        [ a owl:Restriction ; owl:onProperty csf:coreElement ; owl:hasValue "true"^^xsd:boolean ] ;
    rdfs:label "Developmental Window"@en .

frm:Caregiver a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:subClassOf csf:CSFRole ,
        [ a owl:Restriction ; owl:onProperty csf:coreElement ; owl:hasValue "true"^^xsd:boolean ] ;
    rdfs:label "Caregiver"@en .

frm:AttachmentQuality a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:subClassOf csf:CSFRole ,
        [ a owl:Restriction ; owl:onProperty csf:coreElement ; owl:hasValue "false"^^xsd:boolean ] ;
    rdfs:label "Attachment Quality"@en .

frm:EpigeneticModification a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:subClassOf csf:CSFRole ,
        [ a owl:Restriction ; owl:onProperty csf:coreElement ; owl:hasValue "false"^^xsd:boolean ] ;
    rdfs:label "Epigenetic Modification"@en .

frm:HPASetPoint a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:subClassOf csf:CSFRole ,
        [ a owl:Restriction ; owl:onProperty csf:coreElement ; owl:hasValue "false"^^xsd:boolean ] ;
    rdfs:label "HPA Set Point"@en .

# ==========================================
# TYPE E: CHRONIC IDENTITY THREAT
# ==========================================
frm:ChronicIdentityThreatFrame a csf:CorticoidogenicFrame, owl:NamedIndividual ;
    rdfs:label "Chronic Identity Threat Frame"@en ;
    csf:hasCSFRole csf:Experiencer, csf:Stressor, csf:Context,
                   frm:IdentityDimension, frm:DiscriminationSource, frm:ConcealmentCost,
                   frm:MinorityStatus, frm:IdentityVigilance ;
    csf:pubmedID "24417575" ;
    frm:compoundsWithFrame frm:ChronicSubordinationFrame ;
    frm:typicalCascade csc:IdentityThreatCascade ;
    frm:typicalSeverity csf:Moderate, csf:High .

frm:IdentityDimension a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:subClassOf csf:CSFRole ,
        [ a owl:Restriction ; owl:onProperty csf:coreElement ; owl:hasValue "true"^^xsd:boolean ] ;
    rdfs:label "Identity Dimension"@en .

frm:DiscriminationSource a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:subClassOf csf:CSFRole ,
        [ a owl:Restriction ; owl:onProperty csf:coreElement ; owl:hasValue "true"^^xsd:boolean ] ;
    rdfs:label "Discrimination Source"@en .

frm:ConcealmentCost a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:subClassOf csf:CSFRole ,
        [ a owl:Restriction ; owl:onProperty csf:coreElement ; owl:hasValue "false"^^xsd:boolean ] ;
    rdfs:label "Concealment Cost"@en .

frm:MinorityStatus a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:subClassOf csf:CSFRole ,
        [ a owl:Restriction ; owl:onProperty csf:coreElement ; owl:hasValue "false"^^xsd:boolean ] ;
    rdfs:label "Minority Status"@en .

frm:IdentityVigilance a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:subClassOf csf:CSFRole ,
        [ a owl:Restriction ; owl:onProperty csf:coreElement ; owl:hasValue "false"^^xsd:boolean ] ;
    rdfs:label "Identity Vigilance"@en .

# ==========================================
# TYPE F: CIRCADIAN MISALIGNMENT
# ==========================================
frm:CircadianMisalignmentFrame a csf:CorticoidogenicFrame, owl:NamedIndividual ;
    rdfs:label "Circadian Misalignment Frame"@en ;
    csf:hasCSFRole csf:Experiencer, csf:Stressor, csf:Context,
                   frm:ScheduleDisruptor, frm:SleepQuality, frm:CARPattern,
                   frm:LightExposure, frm:SocialZeitgeber ;
    csf:pubmedID "19255424" ;
    frm:typicalCascade csc:CircadianMisalignmentCascade ;
    frm:typicalSeverity csf:Moderate, csf:High .

frm:ScheduleDisruptor a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:subClassOf csf:CSFRole ,
        [ a owl:Restriction ; owl:onProperty csf:coreElement ; owl:hasValue "true"^^xsd:boolean ] ;
    rdfs:label "Schedule Disruptor"@en .

frm:SleepQuality a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:subClassOf csf:CSFRole ,
        [ a owl:Restriction ; owl:onProperty csf:coreElement ; owl:hasValue "true"^^xsd:boolean ] ;
    rdfs:label "Sleep Quality"@en .

frm:CARPattern a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:subClassOf csf:CSFRole ,
        [ a owl:Restriction ; owl:onProperty csf:coreElement ; owl:hasValue "false"^^xsd:boolean ] ;
    rdfs:label "CAR Pattern"@en .

frm:LightExposure a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:subClassOf csf:CSFRole ,
        [ a owl:Restriction ; owl:onProperty csf:coreElement ; owl:hasValue "false"^^xsd:boolean ] ;
    rdfs:label "Light Exposure"@en .

frm:SocialZeitgeber a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:subClassOf csf:CSFRole ,
        [ a owl:Restriction ; owl:onProperty csf:coreElement ; owl:hasValue "false"^^xsd:boolean ] ;
    rdfs:label "Social Zeitgeber"@en .

# ==========================================
# TYPE G: SOCIAL DISCONNECTION
# ==========================================
frm:SocialDisconnectionFrame a csf:CorticoidogenicFrame, owl:NamedIndividual ;
    rdfs:label "Social Disconnection Frame"@en ;
    csf:hasCSFRole csf:Experiencer, csf:Stressor, csf:Context,
                   frm:SocialNetworkSize, frm:SocialIntegration, frm:PerceivedLoneliness,
                   frm:CoRegulationPartner, frm:SocialRejection ;
    csf:pubmedID "17854483" ;
    frm:compoundsWithFrame frm:CircadianMisalignmentFrame ;
    frm:typicalCascade csc:SocialDisconnectionCascade ;
    frm:typicalSeverity csf:Moderate, csf:High .

frm:SocialNetworkSize a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:subClassOf csf:CSFRole ,
        [ a owl:Restriction ; owl:onProperty csf:coreElement ; owl:hasValue "true"^^xsd:boolean ] ;
    rdfs:label "Social Network Size"@en .

frm:SocialIntegration a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:subClassOf csf:CSFRole ,
        [ a owl:Restriction ; owl:onProperty csf:coreElement ; owl:hasValue "true"^^xsd:boolean ] ;
    rdfs:label "Social Integration"@en .

frm:PerceivedLoneliness a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:subClassOf csf:CSFRole ,
        [ a owl:Restriction ; owl:onProperty csf:coreElement ; owl:hasValue "false"^^xsd:boolean ] ;
    rdfs:label "Perceived Loneliness"@en .

frm:CoRegulationPartner a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:subClassOf csf:CSFRole ,
        [ a owl:Restriction ; owl:onProperty csf:coreElement ; owl:hasValue "false"^^xsd:boolean ] ;
    rdfs:label "Co-Regulation Partner"@en .

frm:SocialRejection a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:subClassOf csf:CSFRole ,
        [ a owl:Restriction ; owl:onProperty csf:coreElement ; owl:hasValue "false"^^xsd:boolean ] ;
    rdfs:label "Social Rejection"@en .